A consumer can run an event again after failure. Processing guarantees inside one store do not cover every external side [effect](/lore/effect-basics).

> In an idempotent system, the outcome of processing a message once is identical to the outcome of processing it multiple times.

Source: [Q10](/lore/durability-bibliography#q10); [B5](/lore/durability-bibliography#b5-building-event-driven-microservices), [B6](/lore/durability-bibliography#b6-fundamentals-of-data-engineering).

## Failure it prevents

A response disappears after a remote write succeeds, and retry repeats the write.

## Our Effect 4.0.0 reading

`Workflow` identity and `Activity.idempotencyKey` name work. Receiver-side keys or transactional dedupe must enforce the repeated effect’s semantics.

Source: `packages/effect/src/workflow/Workflow.ts`, `packages/effect/src/workflow/Activity.ts`, `packages/effect/src/workflow/DurableQueue.ts`.

## How to check

Lose the response after remote success. Retry the same identity and inspect the authoritative result. This check is our proposal. The books do not prescribe it.

Continue with [Checkpoints follow the promised commit](/lore/checkpoints-follow-commits), [Cleanup can be an idempotent postcondition](/lore/cleanup-can-be-an-idempotent-postcondition).

